<h1>Peter Gonzales</h1>
<p>Chicago Board of Education, District 3a, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026.</p>
<p><a href="https://petefor3a.com" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (petefor3a.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Gonzales says he is running for budgets you can actually read before anyone asks for another dollar, manageable class sizes and real backing for teachers, and fully resourced schools across District 3A, not just the ones with the loudest voice. He says a child&#39;s education should not hinge on whether their family speaks English, can afford extra costs, or has time to decode confusing paperwork, and that kids need someone at the table who answers to them, not to City Hall.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Gonzales describes a career in advocacy work, including helping veterans denied benefits, assisting immigrants with complex paperwork, and supporting domestic violence survivors.</p>
